('neco','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','A policy aimed at controlling money supply to support low and stable inflation is an example of:','[{"id":"A","text":"Town planning"},{"id":"B","text":"Industrial design"},{"id":"C","text":"Civil registration"},{"id":"D","text":"Monetary policy"}]'::jsonb,'D','CBN explains monetary policy in terms of influencing money supply, price stability and growth.','medium','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','At the CBN Monetary Policy Committee meeting of 21-22 September 2026, what Monetary Policy Rate was announced?','[{"id":"A","text":"18%"},{"id":"B","text":"30%"},{"id":"C","text":"23%"},{"id":"D","text":"26.5%"}]'::jsonb,'C','The CBN announced an MPR of 23% at its September 21-22, 2026 MPC meeting.','hard','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','At the September 2026 CBN MPC meeting, the Cash Reserve Requirement for Deposit Money Banks was retained at:','[{"id":"A","text":"23%"},{"id":"B","text":"45%"},{"id":"C","text":"16%"},{"id":"D","text":"75%"}]'::jsonb,'B','The CBN retained the CRR for Deposit Money Banks at 45%.','hard','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','Inflation targeting is best described as a framework in which a central bank:','[{"id":"A","text":"Eliminates all commercial banks"},{"id":"B","text":"Sets company profit margins"},{"id":"C","text":"Announces an inflation target and commits policy toward achieving it"},{"id":"D","text":"Fixes every market price directly"}]'::jsonb,'C','CBN describes inflation targeting as a forward-looking framework centred on an announced inflation target.','medium','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','The Monetary Policy Committee is associated primarily with decisions about:','[{"id":"A","text":"Local building approval"},{"id":"B","text":"Monetary policy settings"},{"id":"C","text":"National school curricula"},{"id":"D","text":"Motor vehicle registration"}]'::jsonb,'B','The MPC deliberates on monetary-policy settings.','medium','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','Which concept is most directly associated with preserving the purchasing power of money?','[{"id":"A","text":"Land registration"},{"id":"B","text":"Price stability"},{"id":"C","text":"Population census"},{"id":"D","text":"Trade licensing"}]'::jsonb,'B','Price stability helps preserve the purchasing power of money.','medium','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','Which institution is responsible for monetary policy in Nigeria?','[{"id":"A","text":"National Population Commission"},{"id":"B","text":"Federal Road Safety Corps"},{"id":"C","text":"Corporate Affairs Commission"},{"id":"D","text":"Central Bank of Nigeria"}]'::jsonb,'D','Nigeria''s monetary policy is conducted by the Central Bank of Nigeria.','medium','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','Which macroeconomic problem directly reduces the purchasing power of money when prices rise persistently?','[{"id":"A","text":"Inflation"},{"id":"B","text":"Deforestation"},{"id":"C","text":"Urbanisation"},{"id":"D","text":"Privatisation"}]'::jsonb,'A','Inflation is a sustained rise in the general price level and reduces purchasing power.','medium','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','Which objective is a core goal of monetary policy according to the Central Bank of Nigeria?','[{"id":"A","text":"Price stability through low and stable inflation"},{"id":"B","text":"Setting school examination timetables"},{"id":"C","text":"Issuing international passports"},{"id":"D","text":"Managing local government elections"}]'::jsonb,'A','CBN identifies price stability and control of inflation as central monetary-policy goals.','medium','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','Which of the following is a monetary-policy instrument in Nigeria?','[{"id":"A","text":"Monetary Policy Rate"},{"id":"B","text":"Import manifest"},{"id":"C","text":"Building permit"},{"id":"D","text":"Vehicle licence"}]'::jsonb,'A','The Monetary Policy Rate is a key monetary-policy instrument.','medium','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','Which outcome is generally consistent with successful price stability?','[{"id":"A","text":"Unlimited money creation"},{"id":"B","text":"Abolition of all interest rates"},{"id":"C","text":"Low and stable inflation"},{"id":"D","text":"Persistent rapid price increases"}]'::jsonb,'C','Price stability means keeping inflation low and stable.','medium','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','Why does a central bank pursue price stability?','[{"id":"A","text":"To fix all wages permanently"},{"id":"B","text":"To abolish taxes"},{"id":"C","text":"To replace commercial law"},{"id":"D","text":"To support stable economic conditions and preserve money''s value"}]'::jsonb,'D','Price stability is a central monetary-policy objective that supports stable economic activity.','medium','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','A key purpose of clean water in livestock management is to support:','[{"id":"A","text":"Rusting of equipment"},{"id":"B","text":"Soil erosion"},{"id":"C","text":"Seed dormancy"},{"id":"D","text":"Health, growth and reproduction"}]'::jsonb,'D','Good feed and clean water are essential for healthy livestock growth and reproduction.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Crop rotation can help plants explore different soil layers because different crops have:','[{"id":"A","text":"Different rooting depths"},{"id":"B","text":"Identical root systems"},{"id":"C","text":"No roots"},{"id":"D","text":"Only surface roots"}]'::jsonb,'A','FAO explains that different rooting depths allow crops to explore different soil layers.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Leguminous crops can contribute to soil fertility mainly through:','[{"id":"A","text":"Removing all soil nitrogen"},{"id":"B","text":"Increasing soil salinity"},{"id":"C","text":"Stopping root growth"},{"id":"D","text":"Biological nitrogen fixation"}]'::jsonb,'D','FAO notes that legumes in rotations can add nitrogen through biological fixation.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which animal is NOT a ruminant?','[{"id":"A","text":"Sheep"},{"id":"B","text":"Cattle"},{"id":"C","text":"Chicken"},{"id":"D","text":"Goat"}]'::jsonb,'C','Chickens are not ruminants; cattle, sheep and goats are.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which combination lists nutrients animals require in their feed?','[{"id":"A","text":"Only carbohydrates"},{"id":"B","text":"Carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins and minerals"},{"id":"C","text":"Only water and salt"},{"id":"D","text":"Only protein"}]'::jsonb,'B','FAO lists carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins and minerals among required feed nutrients.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which group contains only common ruminant livestock?','[{"id":"A","text":"Pigs, chickens and rabbits"},{"id":"B","text":"Chickens, ducks and turkeys"},{"id":"C","text":"Pigs, rabbits and poultry"},{"id":"D","text":"Cattle, sheep and goats"}]'::jsonb,'D','FAO identifies cattle, sheep and goats as ruminant livestock.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which nutrient group is a major source of energy in animal feed?','[{"id":"A","text":"Vitamins only"},{"id":"B","text":"Carbohydrates"},{"id":"C","text":"Minerals only"},{"id":"D","text":"Water only"}]'::jsonb,'B','Carbohydrates are an important energy source in feed.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which nutrient is especially important as a building material for muscles in animals?','[{"id":"A","text":"Carbon dioxide"},{"id":"B","text":"Protein"},{"id":"C","text":"Water only"},{"id":"D","text":"Ash"}]'::jsonb,'B','FAO animal-health guidance describes protein as a building block needed for muscles.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which of the following is a major benefit of crop rotation?','[{"id":"A","text":"Improved nutrient use and reduced pest risk"},{"id":"B","text":"Permanent removal of all soil organisms"},{"id":"C","text":"Elimination of water needs"},{"id":"D","text":"Prevention of every plant disease"}]'::jsonb,'A','Crop rotation can improve nutrient use and reduce pest and weed risks.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which practice can improve the diversity of soil flora and fauna?','[{"id":"A","text":"Removing all crop residues"},{"id":"B","text":"Eliminating all roots"},{"id":"C","text":"Rotating different crop species"},{"id":"D","text":"Growing only one crop continuously"}]'::jsonb,'C','FAO notes that crop diversity in rotation supports diverse soil flora and fauna.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which practice helps reduce the carry-over of crop-specific pests and diseases?','[{"id":"A","text":"Crop rotation"},{"id":"B","text":"Continuous monocropping"},{"id":"C","text":"Overgrazing"},{"id":"D","text":"Bush burning"}]'::jsonb,'A','FAO notes that crop rotation helps prevent carry-over of crop-specific pests and diseases.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which three nutrients are commonly referred to as NPK fertilizer nutrients?','[{"id":"A","text":"Nitrate, phosphate and kerosene"},{"id":"B","text":"Nickel, phosphorus and krypton"},{"id":"C","text":"Nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium"},{"id":"D","text":"Nitrogen, protein and potassium"}]'::jsonb,'C','NPK refers to nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','aa0c0b77-5601-4bcc-a1fd-9259fee4579b'::uuid,'Financial Statements','A current asset is generally expected to be converted to cash within:','[{"id":"A","text":"No defined period"},{"id":"B","text":"One year"},{"id":"C","text":"Ten years"},{"id":"D","text":"Fifty years"}]'::jsonb,'B','Current assets are generally expected to convert to cash within one year.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','aa0c0b77-5601-4bcc-a1fd-9259fee4579b'::uuid,'Financial Statements','A truck used in business operations and not held for resale is usually a:','[{"id":"A","text":"Current liability"},{"id":"B","text":"Revenue account"},{"id":"C","text":"Dividend"},{"id":"D","text":"Noncurrent/fixed asset"}]'::jsonb,'D','Operational property such as trucks is generally a fixed/noncurrent asset.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','aa0c0b77-5601-4bcc-a1fd-9259fee4579b'::uuid,'Financial Statements','Inventory is generally classified as:','[{"id":"A","text":"An asset"},{"id":"B","text":"A liability"},{"id":"C","text":"An expense only"},{"id":"D","text":"A dividend"}]'::jsonb,'A','Inventory is an asset.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','aa0c0b77-5601-4bcc-a1fd-9259fee4579b'::uuid,'Financial Statements','Shareholders'' equity is best described as:','[{"id":"A","text":"Only bank loans"},{"id":"B","text":"The company''s tax bill"},{"id":"C","text":"The residual interest after liabilities are deducted from assets"},{"id":"D","text":"All cash sales"}]'::jsonb,'C','Equity is the residual interest after liabilities are deducted from assets.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','aa0c0b77-5601-4bcc-a1fd-9259fee4579b'::uuid,'Financial Statements','Which equation summarises a balance sheet?','[{"id":"A","text":"Assets = Liabilities + Shareholders'' Equity"},{"id":"B","text":"Revenue = Assets + Cash"},{"id":"C","text":"Assets = Revenue - Expenses"},{"id":"D","text":"Liabilities = Cash + Sales"}]'::jsonb,'A','A balance sheet follows Assets = Liabilities + Shareholders'' Equity.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','aa0c0b77-5601-4bcc-a1fd-9259fee4579b'::uuid,'Financial Statements','Which financial statement reports cash exchanges with the outside world over a period?','[{"id":"A","text":"Purchase order"},{"id":"B","text":"Cash flow statement"},{"id":"C","text":"Balance sheet only"},{"id":"D","text":"Inventory card"}]'::jsonb,'B','The cash flow statement reports cash inflows and outflows over a period.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','aa0c0b77-5601-4bcc-a1fd-9259fee4579b'::uuid,'Financial Statements','Which financial statement shows revenues and expenses over a period?','[{"id":"A","text":"Share certificate"},{"id":"B","text":"Bank mandate"},{"id":"C","text":"Income statement"},{"id":"D","text":"Balance sheet"}]'::jsonb,'C','An income statement reports what a company made and spent over a period.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','aa0c0b77-5601-4bcc-a1fd-9259fee4579b'::uuid,'Financial Statements','Which financial statement shows what a company owns and owes at a specific point in time?','[{"id":"A","text":"Income statement"},{"id":"B","text":"Cash flow statement"},{"id":"C","text":"Sales invoice"},{"id":"D","text":"Balance sheet"}]'::jsonb,'D','A balance sheet is a point-in-time statement of assets, liabilities and equity.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','aa0c0b77-5601-4bcc-a1fd-9259fee4579b'::uuid,'Financial Statements','Which item is normally a liability?','[{"id":"A","text":"Cash in hand"},{"id":"B","text":"Inventory held for sale"},{"id":"C","text":"Equipment owned"},{"id":"D","text":"Amount owed to a supplier"}]'::jsonb,'D','Amounts owed to suppliers are liabilities.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','aa0c0b77-5601-4bcc-a1fd-9259fee4579b'::uuid,'Financial Statements','Which item is normally an asset?','[{"id":"A","text":"Cash"},{"id":"B","text":"Bank loan payable"},{"id":"C","text":"Tax payable"},{"id":"D","text":"Trade payable"}]'::jsonb,'A','Cash is an asset.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','aa0c0b77-5601-4bcc-a1fd-9259fee4579b'::uuid,'Financial Statements','Which statement is a snapshot at the end of a reporting period?','[{"id":"A","text":"Sales journal"},{"id":"B","text":"Balance sheet"},{"id":"C","text":"Income statement only"},{"id":"D","text":"Cash flow statement only"}]'::jsonb,'B','A balance sheet reports financial position at a point in time.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','aa0c0b77-5601-4bcc-a1fd-9259fee4579b'::uuid,'Financial Statements','Which statement shows changes in shareholders'' interests over time?','[{"id":"A","text":"Bank teller slip"},{"id":"B","text":"Inventory requisition"},{"id":"C","text":"Statement of shareholders'' equity"},{"id":"D","text":"Purchase order"}]'::jsonb,'C','The statement of shareholders'' equity shows changes in owners'' interests over time.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('neco','e3b0d03f-acf7-4ddb-9755-7f4072459e76'::uuid,'Constitution & Legislature','Each Nigerian state is represented in the Senate by how many senatorial districts?','[{"id":"A","text":"Two"},{"id":"B","text":"Five"},{"id":"C","text":"Three"},{"id":"D","text":"One"}]'::jsonb,'C','Each of the 36 states has three senatorial districts.','medium','National Assembly of Nigeria','https://nass.gov.ng/about/item/1548','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
